      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The family of T-cell immunoglobulin domain and mucin domain (TIM) proteins is identified to be expressed on T cells. A member of Tim family, TIM-1, was considered as a membrane protein that is associated with the development of helper T cell (Th2) biased immune responses, and may be selectively expressed on Th2 cells. In the present study we performed single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) scanning of the coding and promoter regions of human Tim-1 gene. We identified a total of ten SNPs including five novel SNPs (-1166C>G, -416G>C, -232A>G, 5365C>T, and 5529A>G) in the coding and promoter regions, one novel variation site (-2278_-2276dupATT) in the promoter region and three variations (5383_5397del, 5387_5389insAAC, and 5509_5511delCAA) in exon 4 of human Tim-1 gene. Our results suggest that the exon 4 variation site in human Tim-1 gene is associated with the susceptibility of allergic disease."},
